{"kind":"report","text":"Technical recommendation for planner decision6e6d8290, completing066095f9/promise71f6fbda. Advice only: not public-contract adoption, Source approval, an enabled route, or a deployment. Basis is landed7a6a1b55 source, reviewed G2q-a/q-b,6e6d8290/cf33e6b6/5081274d and existing69a33abc. Apps review is complete separately; requester has now adopted its C1/C2 refinements inf31290f2, final successor Source still owed.\n\n1. Adopt the exact success body already sized by private q-b: {ok:true,at:head,value:{v:1,scope:fullScopeRef,query:selectionDigest,argument:exactPageArgument,items},complete,next?}. Canonical UTF8 of the WHOLE body must be \u003c=262144bytes, including every field, comma and next cursor. Return those exact serialized bytes, not a JSON-encoded string or another wrapper. query excludes input cursor; argument is the86ASCII-byte G2q-a identity including exact cursor/null and all scope/version/selection/order/limits. Client verifies both, full scope/head, order and next. complete=true means only selected suffix exhausted at this head; next absent. complete=false requires nonempty items and a canonical next at the last emitted ID. No empty repeating cursor, prefix proof, whole inventory or authority implication.\n\nAdopt deferred oversized-row refusal: current page may return its largest fitting nonempty prefix without proving every future row fits. All admitted prefix envelope sizes precede body reads; a later complete prefix may reclaim cursor framing. Never skip the first unreturned row. If next page fits no legal nonempty prefix, return explicit row-too-large (recommended query-specific413 refusal, \u003c=4KiB error JSON, no success at/next). Consumers must preserve incomplete/refused coverage, not present the preceding prefix as complete. Keep G2a1616metadata candidates/128KiB,100row,256KiB envelope caps; do not scan beyond lookahead to prove future fit.\n\n2. Prefer GET /v1/scopes/:scope/query-items?q=\u003ccanonical unpadded base64url of G2q-a canonical query JSON\u003e. Recommend one sole literal q, encoded ASCII\u003c=10923characters and decoded canonical actualUTF8\u003c=8192bytes. Version1/full scope remains inside signed argument; path scope must equal it. Refuse percent-encoding aliases, padding, duplicate/extra query fields, fragments, noncanonical scope/path, GET bodies and other methods; credentials stay exclusively in bounded Authorization (existing Signed cap2055 incl prefix, Session cap4104). Query response/cacheable errors use cache-control:no-store. Current read statuses can be retained; query-specific invalid query/cursor/mismatch/type/state400, stale/wrong resource409, oversized413 and unavailable503 need an explicit finite query refusal type/mapping, rather than silently widening legacy read admission. State-specific reasons/head/cursor only after full scoped authorization; malformed wire may get a fixed state-free400/413 first.\n\nRecommend query URL\u003c=12KiB actualUTF8, with character admission before allocation and strict ASCII q before base64 decode. A bounded frontdoor must precede existing new URL()/URLSearchParams/decode/hash calls, including app/default wrappers. If a common initial URL guard is needed, define its finite cap explicitly and preserve existing routes; do not claim early query admission when an outer wrapper already parsed it. Worker performs only finite routing/syntax/credential extraction and forwards bounded q+reader; object-owned flight begins before decode/hash/signature/SQL. Native16KB URL limit is provider context, not the application proof: [Workers limits](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/).\n\nPOST is not the first implementation recommendation. Current worker.body/boundedBytes cap total bytes but have neither stalled-read deadline nor read/chunk-work cap, and await cancel. A future POST needs native byte-stream ownership transferred into the SAME query owner, fixed total bytes/read-count/copy/decode work, no tee/clone/unbounded chunk list, and pending ownership through actual completion/cancel settlement. Cloudflare documents byte-stream ownership transfer and warns that tee/clone can force buffering: [RPC streams](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/rpc/#readablestream-writablestream-request-and-response). That API fact is not a native lifetime/cancellation witness.\n\n3. One query admission owner for signed AND session paths: one accepted operation per live Scope owner, no application waiter list, immediate bounded refusal for another; one original10s deadline before decode/auth/storage, inherited by every helper and await. No concatenation of independently timed eligible() calls, no recapture/retry/top-up. Timeout completes the caller logically while retaining its pending slot until the real outstanding task settles. Late results do no further local SQL, authority or cache install. Internal receivers use finite relative remaining caps; never pass a monotonic clock epoch across isolates. This deadline covers the object-owned operation and its outbound queue/peer waits, not unmeasured ingress delivery before object entry or physical preemption. An end-to-end HTTP10s promise would need its own explicitly owned admission/cancellation design and native witness. Cold constructor/background maintenance remain separately qualified.\n\n4. Do not compose boolean eligibility with a later page. Refactor an operation-owned prepared continuation, not a reusable grant. After the last peer await, verify the exact unchanged full native frame/head/incarnation/genesis/status/time and whole current support/policy; then metadata/body/envelope work and final MAC/signature/membership/clock/window/claims check form ONE synchronous no-await/no-write tail. No storage/support phase follows the fresh final authority check. That synchronous invariant can avoid a redundant second three-call frame.current() that would otherwise exceed the destination's already demonstrated16-call preparation cap. If implementation needs another await or cannot prove no intervening writes, explicitly account for another currentness phase; never reuse the exhausted16-call budget or silently reset it.\n\nFor sessions retain live→summary, final→items, mixed→both, and extra summary for unresolved native birth. Derive visibility from declared state.final at the supported pin, not which rows happen to be returned or explicit IDs. Empty selection is still authenticated and reveals a head: recommend requiring an ordinary valid scoped session with at least summary OR items (plus existing unresolved-birth summary), or summary-equivalent signed eligibility; never let a vacuous state predicate authorize it. Existing issued-session expiry/controller semantics stay; no new roster lookup or claim.\n\nSigned query must name its own query-items resource and exact86byte argument at admission, preparation and final check. No summary literal as query argument, global 'other read' grant, legacy checkLocalSignedRead recent-history walk, Chains catch-up, or non-genesis causal root. Bootstrap allows LIVE selections only under recent indexed local signer OR exact own-genesis root; final/mixed refused even sparse/empty IDs. G2s unknown is not negative; preserve OR evidence logic and full scope incarnation. Recent-window comparisons are repeated using current request/clock after awaits. Immutable within-operation signer/root content can support those fresh comparisons; it is not cached standing.\n\n5. Explicitly adopt a conservative composed SIGNED ceiling rather than claiming independent1MiB helpers remain a single1MiB operation. Current LocalSigners.proof loads and validates up to one1MiB actor entry, even before returning an old/ineligible result; G2r may load16causal entries totalling1MiB; G2p capture may load own genesis again up to1MiB plus256KiB declaration. These are real separate transfers unless source implements shared admitted bytes.\n\nRecommended named reservations, PROPOSALS requiring adoption and new Source enforcement/counters:\n- indexed signer evidence: \u003c=16conservative SQL/control calls,64KiB metadata and one1MiB entry body;\n- G2r causal phase: \u003c=128conservative native SQL/control calls and512KiB metadata ACROSS caller and trusted exact-proof receivers, \u003c=16entry bodies/1MiB, existing64attempts/512visits/four causal steps and \u003c=16exact proof RPCs; reserve receiver worst case before dispatch, no arbitrary source fallback;\n- ONE local G2p preparation: unchanged16calls/16candidates/64KiB metadata/one1MiB genesis/256KiB declaration, no new borrow/reset;\n- ONE q-b page: \u003c=200item SQL calls (100sparse metadata+100PK bodies worst case), existing1616candidates/128KiB metadata/100emitted bodies and \u003c=256KiB full response.\n\nThus proposed maximum is360conservative calls,768KiB metadata,18historical body selections/3MiB raw history,256KiB declaration and256KiB page response, plus explicitly bounded query/header/proof framing. These are admitted-work ceilings, NOT global heap/copy/wire/constructor/background limits, and not current implemented counters. New native Source must demonstrate every phase/call and no omitted final checks; fail closed at any reservation. G2r's causal1MiB itself is unchanged. ReadPreparation/canonical validators are not free cache-hit work.\n\nPreferred optimization is within-operation reuse of the actual fully sealed admitted own-genesis bytes under full FactRef/hash/seq0/applied/native support bindings, with charged validation and no cross-head/authority reuse. Current G2r caches only minimal root, so that cache alone cannot provide a genesis body to G2p. If reuse is implemented, measure it honestly; retaining the conservative hard ceiling is fine. Re-reading indexed signer proof at final instead of reusing immutable evidence requires another explicitly adopted1MiB/call reservation; do not hide it.\n\nOrdinary sessions retain adopted at-most-two G2p participants, each unchanged16-call/16-candidate/256KiB fold/64KiB metadata/1MiB genesis/256KiB declaration caps, plus ONE separately named page phase above. No causal proof participant or extra peer is authorized for session membership. Combined conservative prep+page call bound232, metadata256KiB, prep candidates32 plus page1616; phase payload limits stay distinct. The already approved standalone sessionEligibility boolean still grants no later query.\n\n6. Before any public read-name/dispatcher/claim change, require one complete Source across bytes/contract/native admission/preparation/final authority/transport and bounded consumers. Native composed witnesses must cover bad wire/header zero protected reads, genuine local and genesis-root cases and incomplete-index unknown, live/final/mixed/empty/sparse, all scoped guard points, full envelope B/B+1 and deferred unfit row, head/policy/incarnation drift and expiry after the LAST storage phase, actual aggregate cold/warm counters including both genesis loads/signer body/proof receivers, stalled/late peer pending ownership and no late caches. Consumers bound response before parse and pages/bytes/time per invocation, retain explicit incomplete coverage/cursor and bounded drift restart; no all-pages default or N+1 detail fetches. Existing RefcountedCanceler diagnostic remains unresolved; no physical drain or deployed behavior inference.\n\nNo project code, test, build, provider probe or deployment was run for this recommendation. Requester adoption, implementation and independent final Source remain owed. Hugh's Cloudflare deployment hold remains fully effective.","body":{"formal_approval":"false","promise":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:71f6fbda0f6f0bf33099e983e72d128c5778af44","scope":"Technical recommendation for planner6e6d8290 adoption; no public enablement, Source approval or deployment"}}